=== Polynomial Hierarchy

$cal(N P)$ can be viewed as $exists x. F(x)$

co$cal(N P)$ can be viewed as $forall x. F(x)$. By De-morgan they are similar, yet are different problems.

From here we have complexity classes $exists x forall y. F(x,y)$ ($sum_2$ and $product_2 = forall x exists y. F(x,y)$ classes) and so on. $P = sum_0 = product_0$ (when there is nothing to prove.)
